# Astraea API env vars.
# Most non-secret defaults live in infra/.env.example (the source of truth
# for local dev). This file documents API-only env vars added beyond that
# baseline.

# Optional: Valkey pub/sub URL for multi-node event fan-out.
# When set, the in-process event bus in apps/api/src/lib/event-bus.ts also
# publishes each trace.created / observation.created to the corresponding
# channel on this Valkey instance, and subscribers listen on those channels
# in addition to the in-process Set. When unset (the default), the bus is
# strictly in-process — single-node MVP. Reuses the lazy ioredis client at
# apps/api/src/db/valkey.ts (VALKEY_URL is the read-path URL; this URL is
# pub/sub-only and may point at the same instance or a dedicated one).
# Wire-compatible with any Redis server (Valkey is the OSS Redis fork).
# Example: VALKEY_PUBSUB_URL=redis://:CHANGE_ME@localhost:6379
VALKEY_PUBSUB_URL=

# See infra/.env.example for the shared SSE frame and execution-admission bounds.
# Provider calls are locally aborted at EXECUTION_ADMISSION_TIMEOUT_MS and poll
# cancellation at EXECUTION_ADMISSION_POLL_MS; neither setting provides atomic
# rollback of a request that a remote provider already received.
